<title>GREECE: AGRICULTURAL BANK/GREECE CUTS DEPO, LOAN RATES.</title>
<headline>AGRICULTURAL BANK/GREECE CUTS DEPO, LOAN RATES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agricultural Bank of Greece</p>
<p>will cut its mortgage rates by 300 basis points along with other</p>
<p>cuts in consumer loan and savings deposit rates, effective April</p>
<p>14, its governor Christos Papathanassiou announced on Thursday.</p>
<p>Deposit rates will be reduced by 25 to 50 basis points.</p>
<p>Consumer loans will drop by 100 basis points, credit card rates</p>
<p>will come down by 50 basis points while loans to farmers for</p>
<p>cultivation purposes will drop by 100 basis points.</p>
<p>The lower cost of money will benefit farmers and</p>
<p>cooperatives by some 13 billion drachmas, Papathanassiou said.</p>
<p>Agricultural Bank will offer the following rate structure:</p>
<p>DEPOSIT RATES</p>
<p>** Savings deposit</p>
<p>	 up to 3.0 million			   9.0   percent</p>
<p>	 over 3.0 million			    9.25</p>
<p>    ** Preferred savings-Demetra		10.0-10.75</p>
<p>	 depending on the amount</p>
<p>    ** Student savings account		  9.0-9.75</p>
<p>CONSUMER LENDING</p>
<p>    ** Consumer loans			    21.0 from 22.0</p>
<p>    ** Personal loans			    22.5 from 23.0</p>
<p>    ** ATE Credit Card			   23.5 from 24.0</p>
<p>MORTGAGES</p>
<p>    ** Mortgage rate			     15.0 from 18.0</p>
<p>    ** Mortgage rates for farmers	     6.6 to 12.25 percent</p>
<p>	 depending on family conditions</p>
<p>OTHER LENDING RATES</p>
<p>    ** Investment loans to farmers	   16 from 17 percent</p>
<p>    ** Investment loans to business	  17 from 18</p>
<p>    ** Farm loans				  15 to 16</p>
<p>    ** Working capital loans		   16.5 from 17.0</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
